message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "Reading the Generator's Handwriting: Tokenizer-Aware Features for Fraud Detection on LLM-Synthesised Tabular Data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Roman
    given-names: Jace
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/z5rcnws7bz-eng/reading-the-generators-handwriting"
date-released: 2026-11-23
version: 1.0.0
keywords:
  - synthetic tabular data
  - fraud detection
  - large language models
  - GPT-2 tokenization
  - target encoding
  - gradient boosting
  - data leakage
  - Kaggle
abstract: >-
  Synthetic tabular benchmarks written by language models carry the class label in the
  generator's tokens. On Kaggle Playground Series S6E11 (credit-card fraud, 699,960 rows),
  re-expressing numbers in the units GPT-2 emitted, encoding them leak-free in-fold and fitting
  shallow additive models lifts a single LightGBM from 0.94674 to 0.95063 out-of-fold ROC-AUC;
  a nested-CV blend reaches 0.95099.
